        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 150 zoom property animatable]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30358</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30358"/>
        <updated>2026-09-01T12:10:18.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">From Chrome 150 onwards, the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/zoom" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">zoom</code></a> CSS property is animatable; see <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5183671737909248" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5183671737909248</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">The <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-viewport/#zoom-property" rel="nofollow">spec</a> has been updated so that <code class="notranslate">zoom</code> is now marked as animated by computed value type.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a new data point for animatable zoom.</p>
<p dir="auto">From what I can tell (see <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1917602" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1917602</a>), Firefox has always supported animatable <code class="notranslate">zoom</code>, so I've marked it as supporting this data point from version 126 - when it was first supported.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
